  "name": "DIBench: Benchmarking Decision Integrity of GUI-based Mobile Agents Under Deceptive Injections",
  "notes": "The commercial-app protocol uses fixed screenshots and context for selection decisions, rather than live end-to-end transactions. Android is supported by the paper's emulator setup. Completion and integrity are distinct measures; no reported scores were reproduced. Basis: complete retained abstract and source-reviewed sections of the exact-version paper (3.1 Benchmark components; 3.2 Instance generation; 3.3 Paired protocol/metrics; 5 Limitations/Ethics; Appendix B (Android emulator setup)); not an entire-paper reading or reproduction claim.",
  "published_at": "2026-09-29",
  "relations": [],
  "review_status": "curated",
  "scope": "core",
  "summary": "Evaluates whether deceptive UI content steers mobile agents away from instruction-consistent choices, using paired benign and injected decision states and decision-integrity metrics.",
  "topics": [
    "evaluation",
    "safety-security",
    "mobile-navigation"
